  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "revolution",
      "title": "The French Revolution",
      "text": "In 1789 hungry people in France rose up against King Louis XVI and Queen Marie-Antoinette. Danton and Robespierre were two of its leaders. In the end France had no king."
    },
    {
      "id": "brioche",
      "title": "« Let them eat cake »",
      "text": "The queen is said to have answered « qu'ils mangent de la brioche » when the people had no bread. She probably never said it."
    },
    {
      "id": "puns",
      "title": "The mice's names",
      "text": "The mouse names are jokes. Un loir is a dormouse, une souris is a mouse, ronger means to nibble, and un raton is a young rat. The game keeps it gentle: no mouse is hurt, and the king only loses his crown."
    }
  ],
